---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Attribution Memory for Shopify - AnalytXpert" description="Make every Shopify order remember where it came from. No apps, no lock-in, no guesswork.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-b from-background to-muted/20">

    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-20 pb-16 text-center">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-primary to-primary/60 bg-clip-text text-transparent">
          Attribution Memory for Shopify Orders
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-muted-foreground mb-4">
          Make every order remember where it came from — so your decisions aren't based on guesses, dashboards, or attribution models.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground/80 mb-8">
          Built for Shopify brands running paid traffic who want reliable order-level truth.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/resources/attribution-memory-script-generator"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-14 px-8 text-lg font-medium bg-primary text-primary-foreground rounded-md hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors mb-3"
        >
          Generate Attribution Memory Script
        </a>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Takes ~2 minutes. No app installs. No lock-in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem Section -->
    <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">
          Most Shopify stores lose attribution at the worst possible moment.
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-muted-foreground space-y-4">
          <p>You spend money to acquire a customer.</p>
          <p>They browse, come back, click an ad again, maybe switch devices — and finally purchase.</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">At that moment, the most important context is lost.</p>

          <div class="my-8 p-6 bg-muted/50 rounded-lg border border-border">
            <p class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">What you're left with:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
              <li>Conflicting dashboards</li>
              <li>Channels taking credit they didn't earn</li>
              <li>"ROAS looks fine, profit doesn't" conversations</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <p class="text-foreground font-medium">The issue isn't your ads.</p>
          <p class="text-foreground font-medium">It's that your orders don't remember their origin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What is Attribution Memory Section -->
    <section class="bg-muted/30 py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">
            What is Attribution Memory?
          </h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-muted-foreground space-y-4">
            <p>
              Attribution Memory means storing acquisition context <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">inside the Shopify order itself</span> — permanently.
            </p>

            <div class="text-center space-y-2 my-6">
              <p class="line-through">Not in GA4.</p>
              <p class="line-through">Not in Meta.</p>
              <p class="line-through">Not in a model that can change.</p>
              <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-4">On the order.</p>
            </div>

            <p>
              So when you export, analyze, audit, or review performance months later, the truth is still there.
            </p>

            <div class="my-8 p-6 bg-background rounded-lg border border-primary/20">
              <p class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-4">Each order remembers:</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 list-none pl-0">
                <li>&#10003; UTM source, medium, campaign</li>
                <li>&#10003; Click IDs (Google, Meta, etc.)</li>
                <li>&#10003; Landing page context</li>
                <li>&#10003; Session timestamp</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Proof Section -->
    <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">
          What this looks like in a real Shopify order
        </h2>

        <!-- Screenshot Grid -->
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow">
            <img
              src="/assets/Shopify-attribution-memory1.png"
              alt="Shopify order showing first touch and last touch attribution data in Additional details"
              class="w-full h-auto"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow">
            <img
              src="/assets/Shopify-attribution-memory2.png"
              alt="Attribution Memory captured in Shopify order attributes"
              class="w-full h-auto"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow">
            <img
              src="/assets/Shopify-attribution-memory3.png"
              alt="UTM parameters and click IDs stored in Shopify order"
              class="w-full h-auto"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow">
            <img
              src="/assets/Shopify-attribution-memory4.png"
              alt="Complete attribution tracking in Shopify Additional details"
              class="w-full h-auto"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4">
            This data is attached to the order — not inferred later.
          </p>
          <div class="inline-block text-left space-y-2">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">Once it's there:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground list-none pl-0">
              <li>&bull; Refunds don't break it</li>
              <li>&bull; Exports don't lose it</li>
              <li>&bull; Attribution models don't overwrite it</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why This Changes Things Section -->
    <section class="bg-muted/30 py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">
            Why this changes how you read your business
          </h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-muted-foreground space-y-6">
            <p>When orders remember their origin, conversations change.</p>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
              <div class="p-6 bg-background/50 rounded-lg border border-border">
                <p class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-destructive" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 14l2-2m0 0l2-2m-2 2l-2-2m2 2l2 2m7-2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
                  You stop asking:
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground italic">"Which dashboard is right?"</p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-6 bg-primary/5 rounded-lg border border-primary/20">
                <p class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
                  You start asking:
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm list-none pl-0">
                  <li>"Which channels bring repeat buyers?"</li>
                  <li>"Which products only work on certain channels?"</li>
                  <li>"Where are we losing money before checkout?"</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-center text-foreground font-medium text-xl">
              Attribution Memory doesn't give answers by itself —<br />
              it gives you data you can finally trust.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How It Works Section -->
    <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">
          How Attribution Memory works (high level)
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-8 mb-12">
          <div class="flex gap-6">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
              1
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Capture early</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Attribution parameters are captured when a visitor lands or adds to cart.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-6">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
              2
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Persist through checkout</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                The data stays with the user through checkout — even if they return later.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-6">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
              3
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Store on the order</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Once the order is created, the attribution is saved as order note attributes.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <p>No dashboards.</p>
          <p>No plugins.</p>
          <p>No ongoing maintenance.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Installation Video Section -->
    <section class="bg-muted/30 py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-center">
            Get it all set up in under 2 minutes
          </h2>
          <p class="text-center text-muted-foreground mb-8">
            Watch how simple it is to install the Attribution Memory script in your Shopify store
          </p>

          <!-- Installation Steps -->
          <div class="mb-8 p-6 bg-background rounded-lg border border-border">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4">Installation Steps:</h3>
            <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-6">
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">1.</span>
                <span>In Shopify, go to <strong>Online Store &rarr; Themes</strong></span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">2.</span>
                <span>Click the 3 vertical dots next to your current theme and choose <strong>'Edit Code'</strong></span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">3.</span>
                <span>This will open a new tab</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">4.</span>
                <span>Right-click on the <strong>Assets</strong> folder and choose <strong>'Add a new asset'</strong></span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">5.</span>
                <span>Upload the script file you downloaded</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">6.</span>
                <span>Click on <strong>Layout</strong> folder &rarr; <strong>theme.liquid</strong> file</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">7.</span>
                <span>Scroll to find <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">&lt;/head&gt;</code></span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">8.</span>
                <span>Create a new line <strong>before</strong> <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">&lt;/head&gt;</code></span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">9.</span>
                <span>Paste the code below (replace the filename with your downloaded script name)</span>
              </li>
            </ol>

            <div class="bg-muted/50 rounded p-4 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto">
              <code class="text-foreground">
                {"{{ 'replace-with-the-name-of-your-script-file.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}"}
              </code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">
              Example: If your file is named <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded">utm-tracker.js</code>, use <code class="bg-muted px-1 rounded">{"{{ 'utm-tracker.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}"}</code>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border shadow-xl bg-background aspect-video">
            <iframe
              class="w-full h-full"
              src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Hiee_KFeajE"
              title="How to Install Attribution Memory Script"
              allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
              allowfullscreen
            ></iframe>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who This Is For Section -->
    <section class="bg-muted/30 py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-12 text-center">
            Who this is for
          </h2>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
            <div class="p-8 bg-primary/5 rounded-lg border border-primary/20">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-primary flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
                For
              </h3>
              <ul class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-primary mt-1">&#10003;</span>
                  <span>Shopify brands running paid ads</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-primary mt-1">&#10003;</span>
                  <span>Founders who want clarity, not vanity metrics</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-primary mt-1">&#10003;</span>
                  <span>Teams doing SKU, channel, or profit analysis</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="p-8 bg-background/50 rounded-lg border border-border">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 14l2-2m0 0l2-2m-2 2l-2-2m2 2l2 2m7-2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
                Not for
              </h3>
              <ul class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="mt-1">&#10007;</span>
                  <span>Stores not running traffic</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="mt-1">&#10007;</span>
                  <span>People looking for "better ROAS screenshots"</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="mt-1">&#10007;</span>
                  <span>One-off reporting fixes</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Generate Script Section -->
    <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-6">
          Generate your Attribution Memory script
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-muted-foreground mb-8 space-y-4">
          <p>
            We've built a simple generator that creates a Shopify-ready script based on your needs.
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center items-center my-6">
            <span class="text-foreground">No apps to install</span>
            <span class="hidden sm:inline text-muted-foreground/50">&bull;</span>
            <span class="text-foreground">No lock-in</span>
            <span class="hidden sm:inline text-muted-foreground/50">&bull;</span>
            <span class="text-foreground">You control the data</span>
          </div>

          <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Takes ~2 minutes.</p>
        </div>

        <a
          href="/resources/attribution-memory-script-generator"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-14 px-8 text-lg font-medium bg-primary text-primary-foreground rounded-md hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors mb-3"
        >
          Generate Attribution Memory Script
        </a>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">
          Takes ~2 minutes. No app installs. No lock-in.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground/80">
          This is the foundation for deeper analysis — not the end goal.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Soft Close Section -->
    <section class="bg-muted/30 py-12">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
          <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground italic">
            Once orders remember where they came from, the next step is learning how to read what they're telling you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Layout>
